1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:03,165
By now, you know that
a project manager

2
00:00:03,165 --> 00:00:06,070
interacts with their team
members on a daily basis.

3
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:07,920
What you may not know is

4
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,900
that project managers
are also part of

5
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,995
a bigger ecosystem within their
business or organization.

6
00:00:13,995 --> 00:00:15,825
Projects are not
the only endeavor

7
00:00:15,825 --> 00:00:17,760
a project manager
may participate in.

8
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:20,850
There are also programs
and portfolios.

9
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:24,300
A project is one
single-focused endeavor,

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,000
a program is a
collection of projects,

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,490
and a portfolio is a
collection of projects

12
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:32,215
and programs across the
whole organization.

13
00:00:32,215 --> 00:00:34,255
Think of it this way: projects

14
00:00:34,255 --> 00:00:36,045
can exist inside of programs,

15
00:00:36,045 --> 00:00:38,860
which can exist
inside of portfolios.

16
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,775
Note that I said "can"

17
00:00:40,775 --> 00:00:43,310
because this won't
always be the case.

18
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:45,155
Projects can also exist

19
00:00:45,155 --> 00:00:47,435
as separate, unrelated
initiatives.

20
00:00:47,435 --> 00:00:49,010
But if they're a
part of something

21
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:50,885
bigger within the organization,

22
00:00:50,885 --> 00:00:53,690
projects can become a program.

23
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:56,585
The collective and
separate successes of

24
00:00:56,585 --> 00:00:59,900
all of these three rely on
continuous improvements.

25
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:01,940
So who are the people that manage

26
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:04,975
these various endeavors
and drive success?

27
00:01:04,975 --> 00:01:07,560
Let's think of this
organizationally,

28
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:09,715
starting with the project manager.

29
00:01:09,715 --> 00:01:12,035
A project manager oversees

30
00:01:12,035 --> 00:01:13,610
individual projects and has

31
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:16,355
short-term, concrete deliverables.

32
00:01:16,355 --> 00:01:18,530
The project manager
is tasked with

33
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:21,610
continuously improving
their assigned project.

34
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:24,810
A program manager
supervises groups of

35
00:01:24,810 --> 00:01:27,655
projects, and even other
project managers,

36
00:01:27,655 --> 00:01:30,905
and focuses on long-term
business objectives.

37
00:01:30,905 --> 00:01:33,310
This program manager
is tasked with

38
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:34,824
continuously improving

39
00:01:34,824 --> 00:01:37,345
their assigned
collection of projects.

40
00:01:37,345 --> 00:01:41,110
A portfolio manager
supervises a grouping of

41
00:01:41,110 --> 00:01:43,090
projects and programs and

42
00:01:43,090 --> 00:01:45,395
provides centralized
management to them.

43
00:01:45,395 --> 00:01:48,189
This portfolio manager is
tasked with continuously

44
00:01:48,189 --> 00:01:49,660
improving their
assigned collection

45
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,670
of projects and programs.

46
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:53,200
Different companies may have

47
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,090
slightly different
names for these roles,

48
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:57,490
but the concept is the same.

49
00:01:57,490 --> 00:02:00,910
Let's examine an instance
where these roles directly

50
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:04,400
create continuous improvement
for their organizations.

51
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,010
A project manager
has decided to offer

52
00:02:07,010 --> 00:02:09,020
monthly cross-departmental
trainings

53
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:10,595
to members of their team.

54
00:02:10,595 --> 00:02:12,320
Their team is small, so they

55
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:13,760
figure it's helpful when people

56
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,290
from other departments understand

57
00:02:15,290 --> 00:02:16,990
their workload and processes.

58
00:02:16,990 --> 00:02:19,160
This way, if someone
is out-of-office,

59
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,990
there will always be coverage.

60
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:22,490
After a couple months of

61
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:24,320
these trainings, the
project manager

62
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,940
realizes they not only

63
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,875
improve processes
in communication,

64
00:02:27,875 --> 00:02:30,545
but they act as inadvertent
team-builders.

65
00:02:30,545 --> 00:02:32,360
Because of the trainings,

66
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,935
employees have the opportunity to

67
00:02:33,935 --> 00:02:36,845
interact and to get to
know one another better.

68
00:02:36,845 --> 00:02:39,080
The project manager takes

69
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,805
this info to their
program manager,

70
00:02:40,805 --> 00:02:44,065
and the program manager loves
this unexpected insight.

71
00:02:44,065 --> 00:02:47,090
Now, the program
manager can establish

72
00:02:47,090 --> 00:02:48,500
these trainers across all of

73
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,000
the projects that
they're managing,

74
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,480
making these continuous
improvements program-wide,

75
00:02:52,481 --> 00:02:55,870
rather than
just project-wide.

76
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:59,040
So exactly what would
projects, programs,

77
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:02,485
and portfolios look
like at Office Green?

78
00:03:02,485 --> 00:03:04,130
Getting the Plant Pals service

79
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:06,200
launched and running is a project.

80
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,210
It's short-term and temporary.

81
00:03:08,210 --> 00:03:09,740
Once a service is launched

82
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:12,220
successfully, the project ends.

83
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:14,885
Keeping the service
going indefinitely

84
00:03:14,885 --> 00:03:17,635
requires the project
to become a program.

85
00:03:17,635 --> 00:03:19,230
The program—running

86
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:21,190
the Plant Pals
service—becomes one of

87
00:03:21,190 --> 00:03:24,200
Office Green's long-term
business objectives,

88
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,370
and the company will work

89
00:03:25,370 --> 00:03:27,605
on continuously
improving the program.

90
00:03:27,605 --> 00:03:30,230
Now Plant Pals, along
with other projects and

91
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:31,700
programs at Office Green, are

92
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:33,905
included in the
company's portfolio.

93
00:03:33,905 --> 00:03:35,720
As continuous improvements are

94
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,745
executed in Project
Plant Pals,

95
00:03:37,745 --> 00:03:39,470
the program and portfolios and

96
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:42,055
Office Green will notice
the benefits of that.

97
